<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Belize City</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Belize City is the largest city of Belize, at the mouth of the Belize River on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a> coast. It grew from a settlement of British logwood and mahogany cutters, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baymen">Baymen</a>, and served as capital of British Honduras. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hurricane-hattie">Hurricane Hattie</a> devastated it in 1961, a new inland capital was built at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belmopan">Belmopan</a>, completed in 1970, though Belize City remains the commercial centre.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/belize-city.jpg" alt="Belize City" width="320" height="265" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pgbk1987 · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Belize_City_Montage.jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
